# Snapshots

To switch: `snap <tag>`

---

## v1-menubar-basics

**Menubar usage app (SwiftPM)**

Claude Usage menubar app built as a Swift package: logo icon, popover with session/weekly limits, first-run consent prompt, launch at login, claude.ai sign-in window. Limitations: the claude.ai sign-in and usage endpoint were not verified end to end; no settings window, notifications, forecast or widgets.

## v2-pre-clausage

**Claude Usage before the Clausage rebrand**

Mac menubar app (popover, settings, accounts, notifications, Claude Code tab, Sparkle) plus the iOS app and widgets with the in-app claude.ai sign-in and cookie data path. Feasibility research and the Clausage design handoff are committed. Limitations: the old blue/accent styling, no plan badge, product breakdown, usage credits or weekly history; the large widget's day chart still uses fixture data.

## v3-clausage-brand

**Clausage brand and new usage sections (iOS + macOS)**

Bricolage type and Paper/Ink/Sand palette across both apps; plan badge, Limiting now chip, weekly product split, running-total chart (each app records its own history), usage credits (iPhone), Claude Code contributors pane (Mac), branded widgets, popover, menu bar and Settings. Limitations: App Icon alternates and the privacy-policy link aren't built; some Mac control tints and the iPhone pull-to-refresh were only verified offscreen/in the simulator.

## v4-pre-rename

**Last version with the claude-usage identifiers**

Clausage-branded Mac and iOS apps still built as `Claude Usage.app` with bundle IDs `com.postfl.claude-usage*`, App Group `group.com.postfl.claude-usage`, the `ClaudeUsage` Xcode project and the Sparkle feed at updates.postfl.com/claude-usage. About links point to clausage.ai; `site/` has plain placeholder pages. Limitations: the clausage.ai pages are not uploaded yet.

## v5-pre-ventura

**Multi-account Mac app, macOS 14 minimum**

Clausage 0.0.5 in progress: Google sign-in popup fix, Free plan state on Mac and iPhone, Pro/Max copy on the site and README. The Mac app supports several claude.ai accounts, each in its own `WKWebsiteDataStore(forIdentifier:)`, which needs macOS 14. Limitations: no macOS 13 support.

## v6-pre-ios-main

**iPhone main screen before the v3 handoff**

Clausage 0.0.6 in progress: iOS App Store requirements, sample data mode, tally app icon, brand mark halo fix, gear hit-area fix. Main screen still has the custom header (starburst mark + "Usage"), a hidden navigation bar with a floating glass gear, and the "Limiting now" chip.

## v7-pre-ios-settings

**iPhone main screen v3, Settings before the v2 handoff**

Main screen rebuilt to the v3 handoff (system nav bar, tally title row, runout chip, idle/full rows). Settings still has the old notification names, in-app Feedback and Privacy screens, one app icon (the tally) and no Acknowledgements.

## v8-pre-macos-v2

**Mac app before the macOS v2 handoff**

Clausage 0.0.6 in progress: iPhone main screen v3, Settings v2, pull to refresh, sign-in that waits for the first fetch. The Mac popover and Settings still have the pre-v3 styling: the product line in the popover, no Usage pane in Settings, system blue accent.

## v9-pre-macos-settings

**Mac 0.0.8 shipped, before the Settings v2 handoff**

Clausage 0.0.9 in progress (0.0.8 released): popover and Settings in the v2 styling, native segmented pickers, accent Fill option, release.sh installs the previous release for an update test. Updates still go through Sparkle's gentle reminder (a notification and a popover line) or silent install on quit.
